Full Text of Measure G
City of Los Alamitos
ORDINANCE NO. XX
AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF LOS ALAMITOS, CALIFORNIA, AMENDING
LOS ALAMITOS MUNICIPAL CODE SECTION 3.16.030 TO INCREASE THE CITY’S TRANSIENT
OCCUPANCY TAX RATE FROM EIGHT PERCENT (8%) TO TWELVE PERCENT (12%)
WHEREAS, the City of Los Alamitos (“City”) is committed to preserving the small-town character, public safety services, neighborhood quality,
and fiscal stability that residents and businesses rely upon; and
WHEREAS, the City continues to experience increasing operational costs associated with maintaining streets, parks, public facilities, public
safety services, and other essential municipal services expected by the community; and
WHEREAS, the City operates with limited local revenue sources and must carefully manage available resources to maintain essential City
services and respond to community needs; and
WHEREAS, the City needs dependable and local sources of revenue to fund and to support essential, necessary, and appropriate general City
services provided to the public; and
WHEREAS, over the last several years the State of California has gone from one financial crisis to another with no end in sight; and
WHEREAS, during each of the past several years the State of California has reduced or taken funding from cities, counties, and school districts
in order to fund its deficits and may continue to do so into the foreseeable future; and
WHEREAS, transient occupancy tax revenues, which have been a source of locally controlled funds available to pay for essential City services,
are limited; and
WHEREAS, the State of California has shifted responsibility for many programs back to cities, like Los Alamitos, without the necessary funds to
provide the services residents need and expect; and
WHEREAS, the City’s general fund expenditures are projected to increase due to inflationary costs and unfunded mandates from the state in
the near future causing the City to have challenges to maintain all levels of service and will not have capacity to fund facilities that are necessary to
deliver services that the community desires; and
WHEREAS, transient occupancy tax revenues, which have been a source of locally controlled funds available to pay for essential City services,
are limited; and
WHEREAS, transient occupancy tax revenues generated by visitors staying in local hotels provide a locally controlled source of funding that
can help support general municipal services without directly increasing taxes on residents; and
WHEREAS, additional locally controlled revenue would assist the City in addressing rising costs associated with public safety, infrastructure
maintenance, park and facility improvements, and other community priorities identified by residents and the City Council; and
WHEREAS, California Revenue and Taxation Code section 7280, et seq., authorizes the City to levy a transient occupancy tax (“TOT”) upon the
privilege of occupying a hotel, as defined in Section 3.16.020 of the Los Alamitos Municipal Code, for a period of 30 days or less; and
WHEREAS, many nearby jurisdictions have a TOT rate between ten percent (10%) and fifteen percent (15%). At this time, the City’s TOT rate
is less than each of the following jurisdictions: Aliso Viejo, Anaheim, Brea, Buena Park, Cypress, Dana Point, Fountain Valley, Fullerton, Garden Grove,
Huntington Beach, La Palma, Laguna Beach, Laguna Hills, Laguna Woods, Lake Forest, Orange, Placentia, San Clemente, San Juan Capistrano, Santa
Ana, Seal Beach, Stanton, Tustin, Yorba Linda, and Orange County; and
WHEREAS, the City’s current transient occupancy tax rate of eight percent (8%) is lower than many surrounding Orange County and regional
jurisdictions, several of which impose rates between ten percent (10%) and fifteen percent (15%); and
WHEREAS, increasing the City’s transient occupancy tax rate would help align Los Alamitos more closely with neighboring communities while
allowing visitors to contribute toward the municipal services and infrastructure they utilize during their stay; and
WHEREAS, the City desires to increase its TOT from the existing eight percent (8%) to twelve percent (12%); and
WHEREAS, all additional revenues raised by this measure will be used to fund essential city services in Los Alamitos, and cannot be taken away
by the state or used for other purposes.
NOW, THEREFORE, THE PEOPE OF THE CITY OF LOS ALAMITOS, CALIFORNIA, DO ORDAIN AS FOLLOWS:
SECTION 1. The foregoing recitals are true and correct and are incorporated herein by reference.
SECTION 2. Subject to and contingent upon the voter approval requirements set forth in Section 3 of this Ordinance, Section 3.16.030 (Tax Imposed)
of Chapter 3.16 (Transient Occupancy Tax) of Title 3 (Revenue and Finance) of the Los Alamitos Municipal Code is hereby amended and restated to read
as follows:
3.16.030 Tax imposed.
For the privilege of occupancy in any hotel, each transient is subject to and shall pay a tax in the amount of twelve percent of the rent charged
by the operator. Such tax constitutes a debt owned by the transient to the city which is extinguished only by payment to the operator or to the
city. The transient shall pay the tax to the operator of the hotel at the time the rent is paid. If the rent is paid in installments, a proportionate
