Argument in Favor of Measure G
VOTE YES ON MEASURE G, LOS ALAMITOS HOTEL TAX (TOT MEASURE)
MEASURE
People live in Los Alamitos because it offers an exceptional quality of life
and great local services while maintaining fiscal responsibility. Measure G
is a practical, locally controlled solution that will help protect essential
city services without increasing taxes on residents.
Measure G increases the Transient Occupancy Tax (TOT) paid by hotel,
motel, and short-term rental guests from 8% to 12%. This tax is paid
by visitors staying in Los Alamitos, not by local residents. Even with this
adjustment, Los Alamitos’ hotel tax rate will remain competitive with
neighboring cities.
If approved, Measure G is expected to generate approximately $300,000
annually to support community priorities, including:
• Maintaining 911 emergency response and police services
• Providing neighborhood police patrols and public safety programs
• Maintaining parks and community facilities
• Supporting youth, afterschool, and senior programs
• Repairing streets, potholes, and other critical infrastructure
Additionally, our city will see an increase in tourism as Olympic sporting
events take place in neighboring communities. These visitors bring
increased traffic and demand on Los Alamitos’ city services, including
streets, emergency medical services, and police protection. However, the
cost of providing those services to visitors disproportionately falls on our
local taxpayers.
As costs continue to rise, Measure G provides a reliable source of local
funding that cannot be taken by the State and remains under local
control. Every dollar generated will stay in Los Alamitos and be used to
support services that directly benefit our community.
This measure helps ensure that visitors contribute their fair share toward
the services and infrastructure they use while visiting our city. It is a
sensible approach that strengthens public safety, preserves quality of life,
and invests in the future of Los Alamitos.
Vote YES on Measure G.
